## Verified facts (reuse, don't re-derive)

- `IAbilitySystemInterface` is C++-only. The no-C++ path for a custom character/controller is reparenting to `EnemyCharacterBase` / `EnemyControllerBase`.
- `EnemyCharacterBase` creates the ASC + 4 SEC components (`SECMeleeTraceComponent`, `SECActionSetComponent`, `SECCombatRoleComponent`, `SECReactionSetComponent`), implements 3 interfaces (`IAbilitySystemInterface`, `IEnemyAIConfigProvider`, `ISECDamageable`), and applies a dedicated-server anim-tick fix in `BeginPlay`.
- `EnemyControllerBase` creates 8 default subobjects incl. `AwarenessComponent`; `ThreatDetectionComponent` is **disabled by default**. It does **not** create a `BotStateTreeAIComponent`; `SECBrainComponent` creates that at runtime. It overrides `UpdateControlRotation` and exposes owner-keyed `LockRotationBy`/`UnlockRotationBy`.
- `GA_SEC_Attack` (inherits `GameplayAbilityBase`): plays a montage (random from an array if several), forwards `Event_MontageNotifyBegin`/`Event_MontageNotifyEnd`, and sends the end tag. `GameplayAbilityBase` sends `AbilityEndTag` on end and, via `bLockAIRotation`, casts the controller to `AEnemyControllerBase` before locking rotation.
- `FRangeEval` is a real USTRUCT.
- Scoring in 2.3.0: distance/angle no longer auto-score. Add a Distance Scorer or Angle Scorer to the action's Scoring list. Per-scorer values live in `FScoreBreakdown.CustomScores`, keyed by each scorer's `GetDisplayName()`, folded into the `Custom` factor.
- Debug flags: `ActionEvaluationComponent` → `bDebugLogDecisions` / `bDebugLogExecution`; `MovementEvaluatorComponent` → `bDebugLogScoring` / `bDebugDrawScoring`. There is no `bDebugLog`.
- Distance response direction: `DistanceError = Distance - DesiredDistance`. Too close (error < 0) → the AI RETREATS (moves away); too far (error > 0) → it APPROACHES. Confirmed by `CalculateDistanceScore` and `CloseRangeRetreatBias`. Do not swap these in diagrams.
- Root-motion (evaluate-only) movement is a Blueprint path, not C++: set `bApplyMovementInput` false, then read the BlueprintCallable getters `GetCurrentDirectionAngle` / `GetCurrentDirectionLocal` / `GetCurrentDirection` each tick and feed them to the Anim BP blendspace whose root motion drives the pawn. Badge it `Alternative`, not `C++`.
- All four action-system extension bases are `UCLASS(Abstract, Blueprintable, EditInlineNew, DefaultToInstanced)`: `USECScorer`, `USECGate`, `USECExecutionMethod`, `USECActionHook`. Authorable in Blueprint OR C++, so badge custom subclasses `Advanced`, never `C++`. Override methods: scorer `ScoreMultiplier`, gate `PassesGate`, hook `PreExecute`/`TickExecute`/`PostExecute` (+`bVetoExecution`/`bWantsTick`/`RequestRecoveryTime`), method `BeginExecute`/`TickExecute`/`AbortExecute` + call `FinishExecution`; method definition queries `HasValidData`/`GetAbilityToGrant`/`GetExecutionTimeout`/`GetDisplayName`.
- `CanExecuteAction` / `ModifyActionScore` on `UActionEvaluationComponent` are `BlueprintNativeEvent` (Blueprint or C++), badge `Advanced`.
- Full action score: `SelectionWeight ÷ RiskPenalty × TagMods × Novelty × Chain × Scorers × RuntimeMod × Jitter`. `RuntimeMod = GlobalMultiplier × SetActionOverride`; `SetGlobalMultiplier(0)` blocks all selection. Jitter is deterministic ±5% (`0.95–1.05`) from `Ctx.Seed`. Winner must have `FinalScore > 0`. `RiskPenalty` default 1.0, ClampMin 0.1.
- `FActionSpec` facts: `bEnabled` toggle disables without deleting; `AddTags` applies while the action runs and includes `SEC.State.IsMovementBlocked` by default (that is what holds the AI still mid-swing); `ChainBonusMultiplier` default 1.5; `FActionCooldown.Duration` default 5, `MaxConsecutiveUses` default -1 (unlimited). Distance/Angle/Health/Speed evals on the spec are DEPRECATED (migrated to scorers on load).
- `FRangeEval` presets (values): `MakeMeleeRange` 0-100-250-500, `MakeRangedRange` 300-500-1000-1800, `MakeFrontalAngle` 0-0-30-90, `MakeLowHealthRange` 0-0-0.25-0.5, `MakeAlwaysOne` (no effect). No other presets exist.
- Behavior Tree Sequence method (`USECBehaviorTreeExecutionMethod`) has an `AbilityToGrant` field that auto-fills `AbilityTag`/`AbilityEndTag`; do not omit it. Active set property is `ActiveActionSet` (on both `ActionEvaluationComponent` and the replicated `SECActionSetComponent`). `ChainFollowupWindowSeconds` default 0.6. CVar `SEC.Debug.LogActionDecisions`.
